=== lastn-P1: the natural statement is served by the J1 rewrite ===
== Explain Query ==

=== lastn-P2 (rejection): a LIMIT body without the whole primary key ===
CTE 't' has LIMIT but no aggregate functions or GROUP BY.  Such a body is served as the last N rows when it selects every primary key column of table 'lastn_tx', so that each row is its own group (missing: `event_time`).
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: Non-aggregating LIMIT CTE body does not select the whole primary key.

=== lastn-1: COUNT(*), COUNT, SUM, MIN, MAX, AVG over the newest 10 of 25 rows ===
== Natural statement ==
WITH t AS (SELECT customer_id, event_time, amount, fee FROM lastn_tx
           WHERE customer_id = 3 ORDER BY event_time DESC LIMIT 10)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS n, COUNT(amount) AS n_amount, SUM(amount) AS s,
       MIN(amount) AS mn, MAX(amount) AS mx, AVG(amount) AS av,
       MIN(fee) AS fee_min, MAX(fee) AS fee_max
FROM t;
== Natural statement result (MySQL) ==
n	n_amount	s	mn	mx	av	fee_min	fee_max
10	10	2695	211	328	269.5000	-6	37
== J0 form: same result on MySQL ==
== Query ==
WITH t AS (SELECT customer_id, event_time, amount, fee, COUNT(*) AS grp_rows
           FROM lastn_tx WHERE customer_id = 3
           GROUP BY customer_id, event_time, amount, fee
           ORDER BY event_time DESC LIMIT 10)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS n, COUNT(amount) AS n_amount, SUM(amount) AS s,
       MIN(amount) AS mn, MAX(amount) AS mx, AVG(amount) AS av,
       MIN(fee) AS fee_min, MAX(fee) AS fee_max
FROM t;

